    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Which of the following numbers have 186 as a multiple?\n\n$2,\\ 3,\\ 5,\\ 6,\\ 18,\\ 62,\\ 74,\\ 86,\\ 93$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2,\\ 3,\\ 6,\\ 62,\\ 93$",
      "worked": "The required numbers divide 186 exactly.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}186&=2\\times93\\\\186&=3\\times62\\\\186&=6\\times31\\end{align*}$$\n\nOf the listed numbers, $2,3,6,62$ and $93$ are factors of 186. The other listed numbers do not divide 186 exactly.",
